# How to cite APEX. A placeholder until the paper describing APEX is published: then fill in
# preferred-citation below (and the authors' ORCIDs), so that GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" offers the paper. There, year is an integer, doi has no https://doi.org/
# prefix, and volume and start (the first page or article number) may be added.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APEX, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "APEX: Agentic Platform for Ensemble eXploration"
abstract: >-
  An extensible platform for ensemble history matching, reservoir forecasting,
  uncertainty quantification, optimization and agent-driven decision support.
authors:
  - family-names: Luo
    given-names: Xiaodong
version: 0.1.1
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/lanhill/APEX-public"
keywords:
  - history matching
  - ensemble methods
  - data assimilation
  - reservoir simulation
  - optimization
